  "riskClass": "high",
  "title": "supplier-service auth registration has weaker password policy than main auth-service (8 chars only vs 8+letter+number+common-blocklist)",
  "description": "R6 deep audit finding. Dimension: auth_rbac. Severity: P1. Source SHA: bbd487a3. Scope: R6_DEEP_AUDIT_WAVE. The supplier-service auth registration (line 142-149) validates password with ONLY `body.password.length < 8`. The main auth-service's userService.ts requires: (1) minimum 8 characters, (2) at least one letter AND one number, (3) NOT in a common password blocklist. This means suppliers can register with passwords like 'aaaaaaaa' (8 a's), '12345678' (numeric only), 'password' (common blocklist), 'qwerty12' (may be in blocklist) — all of which would be rejected by the main auth-service. This creates a security inconsistency where supplier accounts have weaker credentials than retailer accounts.",
